    "testable": true,
    "expect": "differs"
   },
   {
    "id": "C4",
    "text": "After the fix, singularize('dishes') returns 'dish' instead of 'dishe'.",
    "source_quote": "singularize('dishes')    # 'dishe'",
    "testable": true,
    "expect": "differs"
   },
   {
    "id": "C5",
    "text": "After the fix, singularize('buzzes') returns 'buzz' instead of 'buzze'.",
    "source_quote": "singularize('buzzes')    # 'buzze'",
    "testable": true,
    "expect": "differs"
   },
   {
    "id": "C6",
    "text": "For words ending in -zes, singularize returns the base form with a preceding vowel (e.g., sizes \u2192 size) and returns the base form with a preceding consonant by removing -zes (e.g., waltzes \u2192 waltz, chintzes \u2192 chintz).",
    "source_quote": "a vowel before the `z` marks `ze`+`s` (`sizes` \u2192 `size`), a consonant marks `z`+`es` (`waltzes` \u2192 `waltz`, `chintzes` \u2192 `chintz`)",
    "testable": true,
    "expect": "differs"
   },
   {
    "id": "C7",
    "text": "For words ending in -ches, singularize returns the base form with a preceding vowel (e.g., niches \u2192 niche, caches \u2192 cache) and returns the base form with a preceding consonant by removing -ches (e.g., churches \u2192 church, matches \u2192 match).",
    "source_quote": "a vowel before the `ch` marks `che`+`s` (`niches` \u2192 `niche`, `caches` \u2192 `cache`), a consonant marks `ch`+`es` (`churches` \u2192 `church`, `matches` \u2192 `match`)",
    "testable": true,
    "expect": "differs"
   },
   {
    "id": "C8",
    "text": "The fix leaves the vowel\u2011preceding -ches case unchanged (old behavior) while correcting the consonant\u2011preceding -ches case.",
    "source_quote": "The `-ches` shape is genuinely ambiguous (`peaches` is `peach`+`es` but `caches` is `cache`+`s`, same suffix), so the guard fixes the consonant class and deliberately leaves the vowel class on the old behavior",
    "testable": true,
    "expect": "same"
   },
